      "title": "Compactness of the minimal elements of quasicomplemented posets",
      "statement": "Let $Q$ be a poset, and write $Min(Q)$ for its set of minimal elements. Suppose that $Q$ is **quasicomplemented** and belongs to the class $\\mathbb{P}^{\\ell}_{MFP}$, and that it satisfies the condition $a.c.$\n\n**Compactness conjecture.** Is $Min(Q)$ compact?\n\nThe question is motivated by the preceding example of a quasicomplemented poset in $\\mathbb{P}^{\\ell}_{MFP}$ without $a.c.$ for which $Min(Q)$ is not compact; the conjecture asks whether the additional $a.c.$ hypothesis guarantees compactness.",
